<title>UK: BGB unit prices 150 mln stg Dec 2012 bond, +45 bp.</title>
<headline>BGB unit prices 150 mln stg Dec 2012 bond, +45 bp.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following subordinated bond, announced earlier by lead manager SBC Warburg, has been priced.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BGB FINANCE IRELAND PLC</p>
<p> AMT    150 MLN STG   COUPON     8.00	MATURITY    17.DEC.12</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.253    PAY DATE   S27.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  50 BP     REOFFER    99.253    SPREAD	+45 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) 10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/GE/IE</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  GERMANY   TAX PROVS   STD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    50 BP     SELL CONC  =	   PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 9.0 PCT GILT DUE AUG 2012</p>
<p> NOTES	S-SHORT FIRST COUPON</p>
<p>		GUARANTEED ON A JOINT AND SEVERAL BASIS BY</p>
<p>		BANKGESELLSCHAFT BERLIN GROUP, BERLINER BANK AND</p>
<p>		LANDESBANK BERLIN GZ</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
